  "description": "KUVKIX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 2/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H138 Co2 N4 O29 Tb4. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.376-5.021 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.56-145.55°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H138Co2Tb4N4O29. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II).",
